==Stations==
Although KTK is a national distributor mandated by the government of Okaiken to broadcast its signals throughout the country, the organization depends on government-controlled local distributors for its radio and television content. These are funded through advertisement revenue as well as 0.3% of sales tax collected each year in the country. All associations' programming is carried on the same regional transmitters, with scheduling coordinated by KTK's Programming Department.

